## 16. HOW TO WORK WITH ME

I am developing this project in GitHub Codespaces on Windows.

My coding level is advanced.

I already have:
- A GitHub repository.
- Node.js.
- An existing PostgreSQL database.
- A Codespaces development environment.

Do not assume I use VS Code locally. I use the browser-based GitHub Codespaces environment.

Use terminal commands appropriate for the Linux environment inside Codespaces.

Do not unnecessarily explain basic programming concepts.

When modifying files:
- Show which files you are creating or changing.
- Preserve existing work.
- Avoid duplicate implementations.
- Keep dependencies reasonable.
- Run tests and validation.
- Report any command that needs my credentials or manual action.

Do not fabricate successful test results.

If something fails, diagnose it and fix it.

If a feature cannot be completed because credentials or external services are missing, implement a clean integration boundary and explain what configuration is needed.

